# vocab/shapes/query-declaration-shapes.ttl
#
# The declaration membrane (R135; spec §4.4, plan Task 2): an authored SPARQL query may only
# name a term one of the owned ontologies declares.
#
# NEUROSYMBOLIC GATE (CLAUDE.md §8) — AXIOM, CONSTRAINT FORM, CLOSED WORLD. This file
# VALIDATES what the PROCEDURAL extractor (tests/query_terms.py) asserted; it never derives.
# The `FILTER NOT EXISTS` is licensed because it is HOLON-SCOPED: the data graph handed to it
# is exactly the union of the non-align owned ontologies — the vocabulary holon — so "no
# triple has this term as a subject" is a closed question inside that holon, not an inference
# from the absence of evidence in an open world. Do NOT build an "undeclared terms" graph from
# this: deriving `?term a etkl:UndeclaredTerm` from an absence is exactly what §8 forbids.
#
# © 2026 François Rosselet · CC-BY-4.0
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#> .

etkl:QueryArtifactShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass etkl:QueryArtifact ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "{$this} names {?term}, which no owned ontology declares" ;
        # SCOPE. The extractor emits EVERY owned-namespace IRI a query names, `prog:` and
        # `docgov:` included, and decides nothing; the choice of which of them must be
        # declared is made HERE, visibly and with a date, rather than invisibly in Python.
        #
        # `prog:` (https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#, 9 terms named) and `docgov:`
        # (https://w3id.org/iladub/docgov#, 12 terms named) are excluded 2026-08-26 under one
        # reason: neither namespace has an ontology file at all, so they are undeclared
        # VOCABULARIES rather than dangling terms in a declared one, and authoring them is a
        # different act (spec §4.1). Tracked as a residue, not an omission.
        #
        # This is a NAMESPACE list, not a term list — no term is ever typed here (G3 / spec
        # §3 I4). It is an ORed STRSTARTS rather than VALUES because SHACL forbids VALUES
        # inside an sh:sparql constraint, MEASURED 2026-08-28 (plan §0.1 F3):
        #     Validation Failure - A SPARQL Constraint must not contain a VALUES clause.
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?term WHERE {
                $this <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#namesTerm> ?term .
                FILTER ( STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub#")
                      || STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub/dec#")
                      || STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#")
                      || STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub/risk#")
                      || STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#") )
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?term ?p ?o }
            }""" ;
    ] .
